        {
          "aiAppOutputSpecification": {
            "dataDisplay": {
              "layouts": [
                "ORA_LAYOUT_MULTIRECORD"
              ],
              "enableActions": false,
              "enableCommunications": false,
              "customNotes": "Using the provided data, compare the new and old figures and present the following:\n\n1. **Display Analysis with a MultiRecordWidget with cols as Metric, \n<PeriodName>: (example: Sep-25),\n<PriorPeriodName>: (example. Aug-25),\nMoM\n\nStrictly always replace <PeriodName> and  <PriorPeriodName>  with the actual period names.\n\n  ** Display a title in 8 to 10 words providing insight of the Gross Margin trend.\n ** Always include a concise text summary (1-2 sentences) that highlights the key insights, patterns, or takeaways from the visualization. Place this summary immediately before the information display.\n\n2. **Format for Amounts**:\n\n   * Convert the amounts to an appropriate scale (thousands, millions, or billions) based on the value.\n   * Include the relevant currency for each amount.\n\n3. **Display Data Rows**:\n\n   * ALWAYS STRICTLY Display ONLY 5 rows with the following metric column:\n \n     1. **Recognized Revenue**,  Recognized Revenue for current period, Recognized Revenue for prior period, (MoM % Change using  Recognized Revenue for Current Period - Recognized Revenue for Prior Period) in a badge with negative % value as red, positive % value as green, no change % value as grey\n     2. **Recognized COGS (Cost of Goods Sold)**,  Recognized COGS (Cost of Goods Sold) for current period, Recognized COGS (Cost of Goods Sold) for prior period,  (MoM % Change using  Recognized COGS (Cost of Goods Sold) for Current Period - Recognized COGS (Cost of Goods Sold) for Prior Period) in a badge with negative % value as red, positive % value as green, no change % value as grey\n     3. **Gross Margin**, same as above.\n     4. **Gross Margin %**, same as above.\n     5. ****DCOGS**, same as above. (Value can be extracted from UnrecognizedCOGSAmount)\n\n\nRules:\n- Format amount values from the raw numeric value only.\n- Amount format must always use K/M/B units only.\n- Do not infer or rescale units from context. Use the provided numeric value exactly once and convert it only by dividing by 1,000, 1,000,000, or 1,000,000,000 based on magnitude.\n- For calculated percentages, use raw input values without rounding, compute the result directly, and display it with up to 2 decimal places only.\n- Do not modify the sign (+/-) for amount values under any condition.\n- Currency must always be uppercase code only (USD or EUR only, based on input currency).\n- Add the currency at the end of each quantity.\n- Examples: 620M USD, 2.3B EUR, 850K USD.\n- Always round to exactly 2 decimal places.\n- Never use more than 2 decimal places."
            }
          },
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Gross Margin"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "end"
          },
          "code": "GROSS_MARGIN",
          "id": "1760660324292",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1760660324294_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "Using the following data, please provide an analysis of the changes in gross margin across different periods:\n\nUsing ONLY the data from:\n- {{$context.$variables.periodName}}\n- {{$context.$variables.priorPeriodName}}\n- {{$context.$nodes.GET_GROSS_MARGIN_SUMMARY.$output.items[0]}}\n- {{$context.$nodes.GET_PRIOR_PERIOD_GROSS_MARGIN_SUMMARY.$output.items[0]}}\n\nAnalyze inventory valuation changes across:\n1. Current period - {{$context.$variables.periodName}}\n2. Prior period - {{$context.$variables.priorPeriodName}}\n3. Current Period Gross Margin Summary: {{$context.$nodes.GET_GROSS_MARGIN_SUMMARY.$output.items[0]}}\n4. Prior Period Gross Margin Summary: {{$context.$nodes.GET_PRIOR_PERIOD_GROSS_MARGIN_SUMMARY.$output.items[0]}}\n\nDisplay the analysis ONLY if at least one of the above data sources is non-null and non-empty.\n\nDo not make up any financial data. Present only what you have access to.\n\nPlease present your analysis in the following format:\nChange from Prior Month: Compare the current period to the prior period.\n\nFocus on key differences, trends, and any significant changes. Keep your comments limited to 75 words.\n\nIf all data sources are null or empty, do not display anything.\n\nIf some data is missing, analyze using only the available data. Do not assume or infer missing values.\n\nDo NOT create, estimate, or fabricate any financial data.\nUse strictly the provided data only.\n\n*If there is no data available to display*, then return a simple sentence indicating that there is no available information at the moment."
            }
          ],
          "outputSpecification": "",
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "agentCode": "ORA_COSTING_GROSS_MARGIN_ANALYST",
            "description": "This agent can take the profit center business unit, cost org, cost book and accounting period as parameters to provide the total gross margin for the specified cost organization, inventory organization or customer level. The agent will also provide comparison of values to the prior period and year-over-year.",
            "name": "Gross Margin Query",
            "type": "REUSABLE",
            "chatHistoryEnabled": true
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "end"
