              "value": "Using the following data, please provide an analysis of the changes in gross margin across different periods:\n\n1. Current Period {{$context.$variables.periodName}} Gross Margin Summary: {{$context.$variables.dCOGSCustomersSummary.items}} \n2. Prior Period {{$context.$variables.priorPeriodName}} Gross Margin Summary: {{$context.$variables.dCOGSCustomersSummaryPriorPeriod.items}} \n\nDisplay the analysis if at least one of the nodes has data. If none of the nodes have data, do not display anything.\n\nPlease present your analysis in the following format:\nChange from Prior Month: Compare the current period to the prior period.\n\nFocus on key differences, trends, and any significant changes. Keep your comments limited to 75 words.\n\n\nRules:\n- Do not make up any financial data. Present only what you have access to.\n- Format amount values from the raw numeric value only.\n- Amount format must always use K/M/B units only.\n- Do not infer or rescale units from context. Use the provided numeric value exactly once and convert it only by dividing by 1,000, 1,000,000, or 1,000,000,000 based on magnitude.\n- Do not modify the sign (+/-) for amount values under any condition.\n- For calculated percentages, use raw input values without rounding, compute the result directly, and display it with up to 2 decimal places only.\n- Currency must always be uppercase code only (USD or EUR only, based on input currency).\n- Add the currency at the end of each quantity.\n- Examples: 620M USD, 2.3B EUR, 850K USD.\n- Always round to exactly 2 decimal places.\n- Never use more than 2 decimal places.\n- Use the current period (<CurrentPeriod>) as the base dataset.\n- Match prior period data to the current period data like a left outer join.\n- Always display for the current period *Maximum 10* records.\n- If prior period data is missing, set prior period values to 0.\n- Percent badges (like MoM): signed value, up to 2 decimals."
