          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1777921638447_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "Using the following data, please provide an analysis of the changes in gross margin across different periods:\n\n1. Current Period {{$context.$variables.periodName}} Gross Margin Summary: {{$context.$variables.grossMarginInventorySummary.items}} \n2. Prior Period {{$context.$variables.priorPeriodName}} Gross Margin Summary: {{$context.$variables.grossMarginInventorySummaryPriorPeriod.items}} \n\nDisplay the analysis if at least one of the nodes has data. If none of the nodes have data, do not display anything.\n\nPlease present your analysis in the following format:\nChange from Prior Month: Compare the current period to the prior period.\n\nFocus on key differences, trends, and any significant changes. Keep your comments limited to 75 words.\n\nRules:\n- Do not make up any financial data. Present only what you have access to.\n- Format amount values from the raw numeric value only.\n- Amount format must always use K/M/B units only.\n- Do not infer or rescale units from context. Use the provided numeric value exactly once and convert it only by dividing by 1,000, 1,000,000, or 1,000,000,000 based on magnitude.\n- Do not modify the sign (+/-) for amount values under any condition.\n- For calculated percentages, use raw input values without rounding, display it with up to 2 decimal places only *without applying any rounding*.\n- Currency must always be uppercase code only (USD or EUR only, based on input currency).\n- Add the currency at the end of each quantity.\n- Examples: 620M USD, 2.3B EUR, 850K USD.\n- Never use more than 2 decimal places, *DO NOT* apply any round for any number or percentage.\n- Use the current period (<CurrentPeriod>) as the base dataset.\n- Match prior period data to the current period data like a left outer join.\n- Always display for the current period *Maximum 10* records.\n- Percent badges (like MoM): signed value, up to 2 decimals."
            }
          ],
          "outputSpecification": "",
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "aiAppOutputSpecification": {
            "dataDisplay": {
              "layouts": [
                "ORA_LAYOUT_MULTIRECORD"
              ],
              "enableActions": false,
              "enableCommunications": false,
              "customNotes": "Build a table by showing the item records on exact customer and item identifiers first.\nONLY Use your source of information to build the table from {{$context.$nodes.MATCH_GM_BY_ITEM.$output.result}}\n\nReturn these columns:\n- Customer\n- Item\n- Revenue (<CurrentPeriod>)\n- COGS (<CurrentPeriod>)\n- Gross Margin (<CurrentPeriod>)\n- Gross Margin (<PriorPeriod>)\n- Gross Margin % (<CurrentPeriod>)\n- Gross Margin % (<PriorPeriod>)\n- MoM (Gross Margin)\n\nField mapping:\n- Customer = CustomerName\n- Item = ItemNumber\n- Revenue (<CurrentPeriod>) = RecognizedRevenue from current-period data\n- COGS (<CurrentPeriod>) = RecognizedCOGSAmount\n- Gross Margin (<CurrentPeriod>) = RecognizedGrossMargin\n- Gross Margin (<PriorPeriod>) = PriorRecognizedGrossMargin\n- Gross Margin % (<CurrentPeriod>)= RecGrossMarginPercent\n- Gross Margin % (<PriorPeriod>) = PriorRecGrossMarginPercent\n- MoM (Gross Margin) = MoMGrossMarginPercent\n    - MoM should always be shown as a percentage badge, signed, up to 2 decimals.\n    - Do not apply any round for the percentage.\n    - If MoM value is null, then display N/A\n    - For MoM (Gross Margin) -> in a badge with negative % value as red, positive % value as green, no change % value as grey.\n\n\nUse the current period as the driving dataset. For each inventory in the current period, attempt to find a matching prior-period record. If no match is found, retain the current-period row and leave prior-period fields blank. Exclude inventories that appear only in the prior period. Never aggregate records, never duplicate rows, and never change the sign of any amounts.\n\nRules:\n- Never change the sign of any amount.\n- Never duplicate a matched row.\n- If only one side exists, keep that row and leave the missing columns blank.\n- Sort in descending way by the value of the column 'MoM (Gross Margin)'\n- Percent badges: signed value, up to 2 decimals.\n- If any value is null, replace it with 'N/A' instead of null or zero, or '0'.\n- Do not round. Do not infer additional decimals.\n- If more than 2 decimals exist, truncate to 2 decimals for display only.\n- If 2 or fewer decimals exist, preserve them exactly."
            }
          },
